        <oboInOwl:id>MOD:00420</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>From DeltaMass: References: The conversion of glutamic acid to pyroglutamic was reported for the beta-amyloid protein. Miller et al. Arch. Biochem. Biophy. (1993) 301, 41-52 [DeltaMass]. The modification in amyloid protein is probably an artifact of treatment with strong acid under anhydrous conditions. Peptides with N-terminal glutamic acid isolated from single cells of Aplysia neurons show partial conversion to pyroglutamic acid, possibly dependent on a temperature sensitive factor [JSG].</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>2-pyrrolidone-5-carboxylic acid (Glu)</rdfs:label>
