        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>PSI-MOD</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MOD:00983</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>From DeltaMass: Average Mass: 67 Average Mass Change:67 References:http://www.abrf.org/archives/hmail/0008/0007.html Notes:1.) Get rid of the DBU. It can cause piperidine amides at Asp residues. The tbu ester side chain comes off during synthesis and the residue is trans-amidated with piperidine (+67Da by MS). If you haven&apos;t yet seen this, you will. Even &quot;normal&quot; 20% pip/DMF (NMP) will cause this, but less frequently. Literature exists for this; I don&apos;t remember the exact reference. David H. Singleton Scientist Pfizer Central Research PO Box 8118-101 Eastern Point Road Groton, CT 06340 (860)441-4404.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Asp transamidation with piperidine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MOD_00983"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>modification from DeltaMass</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DeltaMass:67</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


