        <rdfs:comment>This modification occurs naturally in two forms. At an interior peptide location (MOD:00270) it exists as aminoethanethionic acid, or aminoethanethioic O-acid. At the C-terminal (MOD:01623) it exists as aminoethanethiolic acid, or aminoethanethioic S-acid [JSG].</rdfs:comment>
